{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_07e0271147c8c75f6824a20937b4c70c82c77cf3c5f074596abbac3fe8802acd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Since v4.4.3, default tool outputs are kept small (tighter read_file/run_command output, smaller read_many batch caps) to reduce ChatGPT Web lag, with per-call parameters like max_chars and head_lines to raise limits."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2d672b780cbd6dc2dfce77fb59f27ff545a3a5ab58ade77206ce54ee431258c8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An Electron tray app for Windows and macOS acts as a GUI supervisor for the same local server and tunnel, storing secrets with Windows DPAPI or macOS Keychain."},{"claim_ids":["clm_35146fba8236a8e469ca6b2745b58a22746d95c2fa20eed48bcd94d1215741c4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent cannot read or replace ChatGPT Web's internal context window; it only estimates MCP tool-traffic pressure, not actual token or context-window usage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_437f2da30ba5cd49970f41a3ede7b033354b906c8fa17402c4d7c4eaca0f8057"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project turns a machine into a local MCP coding workspace for AI agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, ChatGPT Web), licensed AGPL-3.0-or-later as a Community Edition; the latest stable release is v5.0.1."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4816bb6f39271ce632c9df6825326e4c2271d3181868f044e170fd734540184f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project requires Node.js >= 18, and the proprietary tunnel client is user-supplied rather than bundled in releases."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4aed66098a4dceab0d94a3238a002c95c66a500a0d4a01f9802c970f3f512325"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A CLI (scripts/lca) offers install/setup/start lifecycle commands plus status, doctor, update, skills, open, stop, logs, and url subcommands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_64d622a49b09798748c876e8da5bd7862de3802f9dbf1c746d9383af55607964"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"compact_context stores a local structured checkpoint (goal, decisions, tasks, git state) under server/data/ with best-effort credential redaction, and resume_context loads it in a fresh chat."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7b1100b6207b80961552b6cafa826975ebaf8573009a1fc501124bbba1b1dc9b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: server tests run from the server directory via npm run test:agent, test:pro, test:security, test:hardening, and npm run eval; the tray app builds with dotnet build."},{"claim_ids":["clm_89579bb0a3b7e75dfbf98f5c07f2a9fe61367af88859ad0add90cc312b958728"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product runs a local MCP server at http://127.0.0.1:8787/mcp, with a /healthz health endpoint and a dashboard at http://127.0.0.1:8790/ui."},{"claim_ids":["clm_af807de68fb2f81d33ce10fe4db442f60accc29a0e124251de1729090c4cae7a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Shipped helper scripts include local-coding-agent.mjs (prompt/setup-wizard/skills doctor), network-doctor.mjs, and support-report.mjs, which writes a redacted support-report.txt without keys or tokens."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b6001a12496929674c33d85d51307cafcf0836a238c92edd75a8968d7841a6b7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Recommended safety defaults are AGENT_MODE=safe, AGENT_POLICY=balanced, and DASHBOARD_PORT=8790; file tools are confined to configured workspace roots and risky actions require local approval under balanced policy."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fc73aadc7a904f5079a9bb70230080f4a80b0837598ad3805945390ca30dd5ad"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The MCP tool surface includes workspace tools (workspace_info, workspace_snapshot, repo_map), file tools (read_file, write_file, apply_patch), search, command execution, git, and approval tools such as request_approval."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fe9793973a4e6b5921fcdfd551c1e2ee7adb2aaf4c9203dc8075137b0c513aef"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool can run commands on the host and is explicitly not an OS sandbox; the README advises connecting only trusted workspaces and using a VM/container for untrusted repositories."}],"claim_ids":["clm_07e0271147c8c75f6824a20937b4c70c82c77cf3c5f074596abbac3fe8802acd","clm_2d672b780cbd6dc2dfce77fb59f27ff545a3a5ab58ade77206ce54ee431258c8","clm_35146fba8236a8e469ca6b2745b58a22746d95c2fa20eed48bcd94d1215741c4","clm_437f2da30ba5cd49970f41a3ede7b033354b906c8fa17402c4d7c4eaca0f8057","clm_4816bb6f39271ce632c9df6825326e4c2271d3181868f044e170fd734540184f","clm_4aed66098a4dceab0d94a3238a002c95c66a500a0d4a01f9802c970f3f512325","clm_64d622a49b09798748c876e8da5bd7862de3802f9dbf1c746d9383af55607964","clm_7b1100b6207b80961552b6cafa826975ebaf8573009a1fc501124bbba1b1dc9b","clm_89579bb0a3b7e75dfbf98f5c07f2a9fe61367af88859ad0add90cc312b958728","clm_af807de68fb2f81d33ce10fe4db442f60accc29a0e124251de1729090c4cae7a","clm_b6001a12496929674c33d85d51307cafcf0836a238c92edd75a8968d7841a6b7","clm_fc73aadc7a904f5079a9bb70230080f4a80b0837598ad3805945390ca30dd5ad","clm_fe9793973a4e6b5921fcdfd551c1e2ee7adb2aaf4c9203dc8075137b0c513aef"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:07:16Z","created_by_operation":"op_bc6d55fd3dbb467a9391cbb738906c30","id":"pg_04cfdc9de28f5302b63e02ccf00a85c6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/longngn204-local-coding-agent-readme-md-95144e610ddc-02ccf00a85c6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_dd0ab0ca85d75acb8744477fe085cd7e"],"title":"LongNgn204/local-coding-agent/README.md @ 95144e610ddc","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:07:16Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bc6d55fd3dbb467a9391cbb738906c30"}
